            <ArticleTitle>Calcifying supracoracoid bursitis as a cause of chronic shoulder pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>758-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of chronic shoulder pain is reported with marked limitation of both active and passive elevations and a normal range of motion of the glenohumeral joint. X-ray examination demonstrated cloudy calcification in the coracoclavicular region, presumably indicating calcifying supracoracoid bursitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
